-d8f2-4ca8-888a-c547a4687610",0,"c4fe7878-2e77-4e00-b47d-fd81d3503db5",0,"INTERFACE (ITcVnImage)"],[254,"404aaf78-a07a-4c73-97fa-9b1abc529bc8",0,"6d97b69d-6365-4919-b7c8-92bac6512bc6",2,"LREAL"],[256,"6d97b69d-6365-4919-b7c8-92bac6512bc6",1,"62618d8f-023e-4c18-8293-a528ab1f6a4b",2,"ALIAS (HRESULT),DINT"],[261,"955c1374-0e13-400f-8d85-5660d975df6d",0,"0e5ac561-ab16-4598-b04d-a28750c3bda3",2,"LREAL"],[262,"0e5ac561-ab16-4598-b04d-a28750c3bda3",1,"03423c4a-4f88-4536-b775-c8223526981e",1,"ALIAS (HRESULT),DINT"],[263,"1d8774a2-efe3-4a1f-89d3-7cc12a3364bd",1,"559b2a84-d8f2-4ca8-888a-c547a4687610",1,"ALIAS (HRESULT),DINT"]],"groups":[{"id":1,"title":"Process image to remove noise","bounding":[38.19031524658203,278.8687438964844,506.08099365234375,254.4412841796875],"color":"#3f789e","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":""},{"id":5,"title":"Multiply Target by factor for brightness control","bounding":[66.7840805053711,1119.565185546875,372.5025329589844,263.3193054199219],"color":"#3f789e","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":""},{"id":6,"title":"Invert image and derive lowest value","bounding":[815.9097900390625,240.31304931640625,906.755859375,423.6544189453125],"color":"#3f789e","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":""},{"id":7,"title":"Convert to REAL and divide by min value = Correction Image","bounding":[1750.1004638671875,246.66046142578125,670.8485717773438,223.923583984375],"color":"#3f789e","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":""},{"id":8,"title":"Convert Target to REAL for multiplication with Correction image","bounding":[2475.1298828125,480.0057678222656,386.0780334472656,232.694580078125],"color":"#3f789e","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":""},{"id":9,"title":"Multiply with Correction image and reconvert image to 8bit","bounding":[2903.000244140625,290.9029235839844,500.9144592285156,204.9319305419922],"color":"#3f789e","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":""},{"id":10,"title":"METHOD 1 - Faster less stable  method - Subtract backround from image","bounding":[1872.9442138671875,913.8948364257812,1595.1732177734375,458.0198669433594],"color":"#a1309b","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":""},{"id":11,"title":"Subtract lowest value from background","bounding":[1893.4415283203125,993.9183959960938,710.76416015625,354.0047302246094],"color":"#3f789e","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":""},{"id":12,"title":"Subtract modified background from Target image","bounding":[2873.57080078125,964.4705200195312,564.4702758789062,271.5852355957031],"color":"#3f789e","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":""},{"id":13,"title":"METHOD 2 - Slower but more robust when levels change","bounding":[786.2269897460938,101.29327392578125,2687.559814453125,735.0311889648438],"color":"#a1309b","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":""},{"id":14,"title":"Control","bounding":[3403.374267578125,-294.38616943359375,287.1420593261719,192.43873596191406],"color":"#8A8","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":""},{"id":15,"title":"Uncorrected Image","bounding":[3806.595947265625,-1071.17822265625,3668.185546875,940.300048828125],"color":"#3f789e","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":""},{"id":16,"title":"METHOD 1 Background Correction - Brightness tolerant","bounding":[3797.788330078125,-115.65464782714844,3680.785888671875,906.1563110351562],"color":"#3f789e","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":""},{"id":18,"title":"METHOD 2 Background Correction - Brightness Intolerant","bounding":[3796.39892578125,816.1293334960938,3683.42822265625,904.9368896484375],"color":"#3f789e","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":""}],"config":{},"extra":{"filemeta":{"name":"Background Correction Comparison","description":"Background correction comparison\n\nThis graph demonstrates two methods for correcting uneven background illumination before thresholding. The example image contains a calibration/grid background, a darker rectangular target, and strong brightness variation across the field of view. Without correction, the thresholded image is unreliable because the same grey level does not represent the same material across the whole image. The histogram is also broad and uneven, making a single threshold difficult to choose.\n\nMethod 1 uses background subtraction. A clean background reference image is first processed to remove noise. The lowest background value is found, and this value is subtracted from the background image to create a modified background error image. This error image is then subtracted from the target image. The intention is to remove the fixed brightness gradient while leaving the object detail behind. This method is simple and fast because it mainly uses subtraction on 8-bit images. It works well when the lighting level and camera exposure remain stable between the background image and the inspection image. However, if the overall brightness changes, subtraction can over-correct or under-correct parts of the image.\n\nMethod 2 uses a multiplicative correction image. The background reference image is inverted and analysed to find the lowest useful value. The image is then converted to REAL format and divided by the minimum value to create a proportional correction factor image. The target image is also converted to REAL, multiplied by the correction image, and then converted back to 8-bit. This normalises the image by scaling pixel values rather than simply subtracting an offset. It is slower because it uses REAL image conversion and multiplication, but it is more tolerant of gradual lighting level changes.\n\nThe left comparison section shows the practical result. After correction, the grid and background are more even, the target separates more clearly, and the histogram becomes easier to threshold. The key training point is that background correction should be judged by the quality of the final thresholded image, not just by how visually flat the grey image appears.","tags":[]},"annotations_plugin":[],"ds":{"scale":0.25249310378034184,"offset":[-837.6544399633324,811.7355979084741]},"linkExtensions":[{"id":171,"parentId":4},{"id":226,"parentId":1},{"id":227,"parentId":1},{"id":228,"parentId":2},{"id":230,"parentId":3},{"id":231,"parentId":2},{"id":261,"parentId":5}],"reroutes":[{"id":1,"pos":[1840.3623046875,885.1939697265625],"linkIds":[226,227,228,230,231]},{"id":2,"parentId":1,"pos":[3670.56005859375,-989.5028076171875],"linkIds":[228,230,231]},{"id":3,"parentId":2,"pos":[6233.82470703125,-1069.128662109375],"linkIds":[230]},{"id":4,"pos":[726.6580200195312,347.2834167480469],"linkIds":[171]},{"id":5,"pos":[44.40347671508789,-154.50228881835938],"linkIds":[261]}]},"version":0.4,"uuid":"b39dd8c0-581a-4ae3-ae19-52bac9353652"}